  "body": "<br/>\r\n<div align=\"center\">\r\n  <img src=\"https://homarr.dev/img/logo.png\" height=\"80\" alt=\"\" />\r\n  <h3>Homarr</h3>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n## Why was this PR needed?\r\n\r\nCloses #3371.\r\n\r\nBoard background video uploads were not working because the upload path treated board backgrounds as image-only media. The frontend file picker only accepted image MIME types, and the backend media upload validator rejected video MIME types such as `video/mp4`. During investigation, I found that Homarr already had a `BoardBackgroundVideo` renderer for video URLs, but uploaded local media URLs did not include file extensions, so uploaded videos also needed extension-aware local URLs to trigger the existing renderer.\r\n\r\n## What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nThis PR adds MP4 and WebM support for uploaded board backgrounds. It updates media upload validation to allow `video/mp4` and `video/webm`, lets the board background upload control accept videos, keeps shared upload defaults image-only for icon-related flows, and makes local uploaded media URLs include the source file extension when returned to the UI. It also prevents uploaded videos from being indexed as local icons and updates media previews/management views to handle video media.\r\n\r\n## What are the relevant issue numbers?\r\n\r\nCloses #3371\r\n\r\n## Why this approach?\r\n\r\nThe existing board background renderer already supported video URLs, so this PR reuses that behavior instead of introducing a separate rendering system. The shared `UploadMedia` component now accepts an optional MIME list, but defaults to image-only so existing icon picker and media upload flows stay conservative. Board background upload opts into the broader media list because that is the only flow that needs video support.\r\n\r\n## Before / After Evidence\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n- `.mp4` files could not be selected from the board background upload file picker.\r\n- If a video reached the upload endpoint, validation rejected it with `invalidFileType`.\r\n- Uploaded local media URLs had no extension, so the existing video renderer would not detect them as videos.\r\n\r\nAfter:\r\n- Confirmed manually on localhost that an `.mp4` file can be selected, uploaded, saved as the board background, and rendered visibly on the board page.\r\n- Validation tests confirm MP4/WebM uploads are accepted.\r\n- Regression tests confirm existing image MIME types still pass.\r\n- Edge-case tests confirm unsupported file types and files larger than 32 MB are still rejected.\r\n- \r\n![Video background rendered on Homarr dashboard] (\r\n<img width=\"1440\" height=\"900\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-30 at 2 32 57\u202fPM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4106af14-c96b-42b3-b61d-37fa05bda10e\" />\r\n)\r\n\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nAdded/updated `packages/validation/src/media.spec.ts` to cover:\r\n- `video/mp4` and `video/webm` uploads are accepted\r\n- Existing supported image MIME types still pass\r\n- Unsupported file types fail with `invalidFileType`\r\n- Files larger than 32 MB fail with `fileTooLarge`\r\n\r\nCommands run:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npnpm exec vitest run packages/validation/src/media.spec.ts\r\npnpm -F @homarr/validation typecheck\r\npnpm -F @homarr/forms-collection typecheck\r\npnpm -F @homarr/icons typecheck\r\npnpm -F @homarr/api typecheck\r\npnpm -F @homarr/nextjs typecheck\r\npnpm -F @homarr/validation lint\r\npnpm -F @homarr/forms-collection lint\r\npnpm -F @homarr/icons lint\r\npnpm -F @homarr/api lint\r\npnpm -F @homarr/nextjs lint\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nHi @Meierschlumpf \u2014 this is my first contribution to this project. I've fixed issue #3371 by allowing MP4/WebM uploads for board backgrounds, updating the background upload UI to accept videos, and ensuring uploaded local video URLs render through the existing video background component.\r\n\r\nWould appreciate a review when you have time!\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\r\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\r\n\r\n* **New Features**\r\n  * Boards can now use uploaded videos as background media, not just images.\r\n  * Media upload and picker experiences now support both image and video files.\r\n  * Copied media links and media previews now work more reliably for files with extensions.\r\n\r\n* **Bug Fixes**\r\n  * Fixed background video uploads failing validation.\r\n  * Improved media display so videos render correctly in management and board settings.\r\n  * Prevented non-image files from being treated as icons.\r\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
